## 13. Repairs

1. Replace the ramp MDR with a constant-severity or derivative-based input that does not grow with horizon; report both finite-horizon power and asymptotic crossing probability where analytic.
2. Increase horizon-seed count or report binomial confidence intervals; add secondary AR(1)/heavy-tail/variance-drift nulls (S2/S3).
3. Keep empirical fixed-horizon calibration only for finite-horizon questions; prefer anytime-valid boundaries (or explicit horizon-adaptive thresholds) for deep-time claims.
4. Explicitly enumerate candidate independent sources (metrology, provenance, intervention, additional causally informative channels) and test shared-failure modes.
5. Separate “recurrence recognition” experiments from “first-time reference authorization / promotion / migration” experiments (S6).
6. After source inspection of actual THDE severity_k, construct matching high-dimensional or operator-level analogs (S9) rather than assuming the scalar absolute-deviation form transfers.

