## 8. Analytic controls

### M4A — Constant-severity fixed point

For

$$
q_{k+1}=\lambda q_k+s,
$$

the exact fixed point is

$$
q_\infty=\frac{s}{1-\lambda}.
$$

With `theta = 1`:

|    λ | Crossing-floor severity `(1-λ)θ` | Below example | q∞ below | Above example | q∞ above |
| ---: | -------------------------------: | ------------: | -------: | ------------: | -------: |
|   .9 |                               .1 |           .05 |       .5 |           .15 |      1.5 |
|  .99 |                              .01 |          .005 |       .5 |          .015 |      1.5 |
| .999 |                             .001 |         .0005 |       .5 |         .0015 |      1.5 |

**[DERIVED]** For this exact recurrence, a positive constant `s < (1-λ)θ` cannot cross threshold from the idealized zero initial condition.

That is a property of the recurrence—not proof that real Nexus THDE receives such a scalar constant severity stream.

### M4B — Normalized linear EWMA effective memory

For

$$
m_k=\lambda m_{k-1}+(1-\lambda)x_k,
$$

with unit-variance iid input:

$$
N_{\mathrm{eff}}=\frac{1+\lambda}{1-\lambda},
\qquad
\sigma_\infty=\sqrt{\frac{1-\lambda}{1+\lambda}}.
$$

|    λ | `1/(1-λ)` | Effective N | Stationary SD |
| ---: | --------: | ----------: | ------------: |
|   .9 |        10 |          19 |       .229416 |
|  .99 |       100 |         199 |       .070888 |
| .999 |      1000 |        1999 |       .022366 |

**[DERIVED]** The normalized linear EWMA has finite effective memory for every `λ < 1`.

Again, this control must not be silently promoted into a description of the complete THDE measurement or hysteresis architecture. The experiment itself explicitly disclaims that equivalence.

